Frequently asked questions

Which German business documents do you translate?

We translate contracts, company reports, policies, proposals, presentations and correspondence. Both German into English and English into German are available. Send your files and we confirm how we would handle them.

Do you also offer German subtitling and interpreting?

Yes, we can support German subtitling and business interpreting alongside written translation. Tell us about your video, meeting or event and your audience. We then advise on the best setup.

Will a native German speaker work on my project?

Yes, our German business translators are native speakers with commercial experience. They match your terminology and tone to your industry. Share any glossary or past documents you want us to follow.

How do you handle confidential company information?

We treat every file as private and limit access to the people on your project. You can request a confidentiality agreement before you share anything sensitive. Tell us about any security rules your company has.

Can you translate German company documents for Companies House?

Yes, we translate company records into English, and we can discuss certification if required. Check what Companies House asks for and share it with us. We prepare the translation to match.
